Komatso Parallel for Hermes v0.21.4
==================================

Observed production configuration (read-only review)
---------------------------------------------------
The current AppData Hermes config.yaml sets both web.search_backend and
web.extract_backend to parallel. Both web/parallel and web/tavily are enabled
and both API-key variables are populated, but enabled/keyed is not the same as
selected. PARALLEL_SEARCH_MODE is advanced. Installed SDK metadata is 1.3.2.
The old web_tools selection code uses the explicit capability backend when
available; with the Parallel key present it does not choose Tavily. Therefore
no komatso-tavily provider is created. This is a configuration/source review,
not a claim that live process state or historical API traffic was inspected.

Preserved provider behavior
---------------------------
The old customized provider calls Parallel.search (not beta.search) with
search_queries, objective, mode and advanced_settings.max_results, capped at 20.
Supported modes are turbo, fast, basic and advanced; unset/invalid mode defaults
to advanced. Extraction calls AsyncParallel.extract with
advanced_settings.full_content=True. Search positions, joined excerpts,
extraction content/raw_content/metadata, excerpt fallback and per-URL errors
retain the old shapes. Both entrypoints check the Hermes interrupt flag first.

Isolation strategy
------------------
Hermes v0.21.4 pins parallel-web==0.4.2 in pyproject.toml and tools/lazy_deps.py.
Both SDK versions use the same import name, parallel; installing 1.3.2 in that
environment would replace 0.4.2 and jeopardize the built-in beta API calls.

The custom provider registers ONLY komatso-parallel. Its Hermes-side bridge has
no parallel import, dependency installer, sys.path modification or access to
the built-in tools.web_tools SDK cache slots. plugin.yaml deliberately declares
no pip/python dependency that Hermes could install into its own environment.

worker.py runs under KOMATSO_PARALLEL_PYTHON, an explicitly selected absolute
path to Python in a separate venv. requirements-worker.in pins parallel-web to
1.3.2 ONLY for that venv. Transitive SDK requirements are confined to that venv;
they are not a fully resolved transitive lock. Worker startup rejects a shared
Hermes prefix, a non-venv interpreter, system-site-package inheritance and any
other SDK version. -I ignores PYTHONPATH and the user site; -B avoids bytecode
writes. The SDK is never imported in the Hermes process. This leaves the
built-in 0.4.2 dependency and both built-in provider registrations untouched.

Each request sends JSON over stdin and receives JSON over stdout. Credentials
are not command-line arguments; worker stderr and exception details are not
returned to users. Windows worker windows are hidden. Each process closes its
SDK client. The parent bounds worker lifetime to 180 seconds and terminates an
async extraction worker on timeout/cancellation. These are intentional bridge
differences from the former cached in-process SDK clients.

Prepared, not activated
-----------------------
No environment was created, no packages installed, no config changed, and no
deployment/restart performed. Future activation requires a separately prepared
worker venv with requirements-worker.in, the worker Python environment setting,
plugin enablement and explicit komatso-parallel selection for both capabilities.
config.example.yaml is a merge example, not a replacement production config.
Until that happens, the prepared provider is not active; the current runtime
continues to use its existing Parallel configuration. No core patch or old
provider.py/lazy_deps.py patch is needed.

Offline validation
------------------
8 targeted tests passed against the v0.21.4 source and real SDK 1.3.2, using
httpx.MockTransport and synthetic credentials. They cover registration beside
the built-in provider, explicit selection, mode/limit parity, real SDK wire
serialization, result normalization, interruption, dependency rejection,
process arguments/credential transport, timeout shape and cancellation cleanup.
Subprocess launch is mocked in bridge tests; no external API, gateway or full
regression is run. Network sockets/DNS are blocked inside the test process.

Reproduce from E:\KomatsoAI using existing dependencies read-only:

  $env:KOMATSO_TEST_HERMES_ROOT='E:\HermesUpgrade\hermes-agent-v0.21.4'
  $env:HERMES_HOME='E:\KomatsoAI\runtime\parallel-v0214-tests'
  $env:PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE='1'
  .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -B -c "import sys,runpy; sys.path.append(r'C:\Users\win-10\AppData\Local\hermes\hermes-agent\venv\Lib\site-packages'); runpy.run_path('integrations/hermes/plugins/komatso-parallel/test_offline.py',run_name='__main__')"

Remaining risks
---------------
The future isolated venv has not been provisioned or exercised end-to-end.
Live API behavior, gateway dispatch and production credentials remain untested.
Per-request process startup adds latency and loses in-process connection reuse;
requests taking over 180 seconds now return a timeout. Worker SDK retries can
occur within that deadline. Error details are intentionally less verbose.
Future Hermes/SDK upgrades require rerunning these contract tests.
